 "description": "Git subprocesses used for revision reads (rev-parse, cat-file -t, cat-file -s, cat-file blob) have no wall-clock deadline. A command that blocks, for example on a partial clone that lazily fetches a missing blob from a promisor remote, a stalled network filesystem, or a hung lock, can pin the calling thread indefinitely. The sc-jev-check command extractor enforces a deadline for its own subprocess, so this is inconsistent.",
